message: "If you use this data in your research, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "Query datasets and run results related to scientific articles about Semantic Embeddings and RAG for Sanctions Name Screening Resources"
abstract: "The artefacts:
           Embeddings related:
           directories:

           query-sets/ (14 query files and sdn_xml.zip, the OFAC snapshot);

           embeddings/:

           results/ (96 raw result files, 13,932 query records) and

           deep-k-probes/ (the k = 10 and k = 20 runs behind Table 10 and the probes Shoihu_UKR_{40,80}.json);

           metrics_recomputed.csv (authoritative point estimates); metrics_entity_ci.csv (Wilson and entity-cluster intervals, Table 3);

           paired_tests.csv (Tables 3 and 4); auc_ci.csv (Table 6); threshold_roc.csv and

           operating_points.csv (Table 7) with operating_points_heldout.csv (Table 8); rank_tail.csv
           (Table 10); latency_percentiles.csv; dataset_audit.csv; and plots/.


           RAG related:
           In directory rag/:

           analysis-rag-gemini-flash-3-6-medium-topk30/ and
           analysis-rag-gemini-flash-3-7-low-topk30-run-{01,02,03}/ — four configurations × 14 run
           directories, containing meta (full prompt, model, effort, token
           usage, timing), ground_truth, results[] of 30 candidates and rag_response.

           metrics_multirun.csv — per configuration × group: recall decomposition, alert rates, override
           and multi-match counts, set metrics, latency and token statistics.

           headline_ci.csv — headline rates with exact Clopper–Pearson and entity-cluster bootstrap
           intervals.

           stability_multirun.csv — per-query verdict and returned-set agreement across the three
           replicates.

           specificity_multirun.csv — paired 2-part vs 3-part comparison with entity-cluster bootstrap and
           distinct-entity counts.

           cases_multirun.csv — every non-trivial case in every configuration, with the adjudicator's
           rationale.

           plots/ — the four figures as PNG."
